    891.7
   ],
   "ocr": "and DC1 vs. one dependent variable, namely CCIt, to look for Granger-causative relationships between CCI and independent variables. The results in Table 5 indicate that independent vari- able C2 is Granger causative of the CCI. Results in behavioral science [28] indicate that people tend to discount older information in favor of newer information. We therefore choose vari- ables that were lagged one and two units for testing. Refering to the results, we add C2 at lag 1 and lag 2 in our independent variables."
